# [Create embeddings]($heading.id('embeddings'))

`POST /v1/embeddings` maps input text to a numeric vector using the loaded
embedding model. Choose `Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-8B` in the
[Embeddings catalog]($link.page('llmd/reference/model-compatibility').unsafeRef('embedding-checkpoints')).
[Any model, any platform]($link.page('llmd/tutorial/start').unsafeRef('send-an-embeddings-request'))
generates an embeddings request with the selected host port.

Both examples request 32 dimensions. The illustrative outputs show the
index, vector length, and first four values using the filter under
[Read the response]($link.ref('embedding-response')).

## [Single input]($heading.id('single-input'))

```=html
<div class="api-example-pair">
  <div class="command-shell">
    <span class="command-language">Request · Shell</span>
    <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy single-input embeddings request">curl -sS --fail-with-body http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/embeddings \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{
    "input": "A generator supplies power.",
    "encoding_format": "float",
    "dimensions": 32
  }'</code></pre>
  </div>
  <div class="command-shell">
    <span class="command-language">Illustrative jq output · JSON</span>
    <pre><code class="json">[
  {
    "index": 0,
    "dimensions": 32,
    "first_four": [0.08, -0.03, 0.14, 0.06]
  }
]</code></pre>
  </div>
</div>
```

## [Batch input]($heading.id('batch-input'))

The generator sentence maps to `index: 0` and the bakery sentence maps to
`index: 1`. The indices are zero-based positions in the input array.

```=html
<div class="api-example-pair">
  <div class="command-shell">
    <span class="command-language">Request · Shell</span>
    <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy batch embeddings request">curl -sS --fail-with-body http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/embeddings \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{
    "input": [
      "A generator supplies power.",
      "A bakery sells bread."
    ],
    "encoding_format": "float",
    "dimensions": 32
  }'</code></pre>
  </div>
  <div class="command-shell">
    <span class="command-language">Illustrative jq output · JSON</span>
    <pre><code class="json">[
  {
    "index": 0,
    "dimensions": 32,
    "first_four": [0.08, -0.03, 0.14, 0.06]
  },
  {
    "index": 1,
    "dimensions": 32,
    "first_four": [-0.07, 0.12, 0.01, -0.09]
  }
]</code></pre>
  </div>
</div>
```

# [Request fields]($heading.id('embedding-request-fields'))

| Request field | Type and default | Behavior |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `input` | String or array of strings, required | Send one nonempty string per vector. Token ID arrays are rejected. |
| `encoding_format` | String, `"float"` | Choose `"float"` for a JSON array of numbers or `"base64"` for encoded little-endian float32 bytes. |
| `dimensions` | Integer, model maximum | Sets the length of each vector. Qwen3-Embedding-8B supports 32 through 4,096 dimensions. |
| `model` | String, optional | May be omitted. LLMD embeds with the model loaded by the server. |

# [Read the response]($heading.id('embedding-response'))

`object` is `"list"` and `model` is the served
model ID. Each `data` entry has `object: "embedding"`, the zero-based input
`index`, and the vector in `embedding`. Entries follow input order.
`usage.prompt_tokens` and `usage.total_tokens` both count the tokens
embedded across all inputs. Pipe either successful float response into
this command to reproduce the output format above.

```sh
jq '[.data[] | {index, dimensions: (.embedding | length), first_four: .embedding[:4]}]'
```

See [Compare texts with embeddings]($link.page('llmd/tutorial/compare-texts-with-embeddings'))
for a client that ranks passages using the returned vectors.

# [Limits and errors]($heading.id('embedding-limits-and-errors'))

These checks apply to LLMD revision `fe922cff`. For example, a batch of
2,049 strings returns HTTP 400 with `error.code` set to `invalid_input`.

| Check | Requirement | HTTP status and `error.code` |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Request body | Valid JSON with `input` as a string or an array of strings. | 400 `invalid_request` |
| Input count and content | 1–2,048 nonempty strings per request. | 400 `invalid_input` |
| Server context | Each tokenized string is shorter than the configured context length. | 400 `context_length_exceeded` |
| Endpoint token caps | Up to 8,192 tokens per string and 300,000 tokens in total. | 400 `too_many_tokens` |
| Dimensions | Within the loaded model's range. Qwen3-Embedding-8B supports 32–4,096. | 400 `invalid_dimensions` |
| Loaded model | The loaded model supports embeddings. | 400 `model_not_supported` |
| Batch completion | LLMD can compute every vector in the batch. | 503 `resource_exhausted` |

LLMD checks the server context for each string before checking the endpoint's
token caps for that string.
